---
/**
 * /stats — the transparency page.
 *
 * This used to embed a Plausible dashboard from plausible.baytides.org. That
 * host was retired in September 2026 along with the rest of the self-hosted
 * stack, so the page rendered a 1,600px-tall empty iframe and its share token
 * sat in the committed URL.
 *
 * The URL is kept rather than deleted: it was published in our own privacy
 * policy, so people may have followed or bookmarked it, and a 404 answers a
 * reasonable question with nothing. What is here now is the honest version —
 * we have no visitor numbers to show, and the things we *can* open up instead.
 */
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';

// The number of listings we publish, read from the generated API rather than
// recounted here, so the figure on this page is by construction the same one
// /data/programs.json serves. generate-api.cjs runs before the build in both
// CI workflows and the file is committed, so it is always present; the guard
// is for a contributor who has not run the generator yet.
function publishedProgramCount(): number | null {
  try {
    const apiPath = path.join(process.cwd(), 'public/api/programs.json');
    const parsed = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(apiPath, 'utf-8')) as { total?: number };
    return typeof parsed.total === 'number' ? parsed.total : null;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

const programCount = publishedProgramCount();

const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Transparency"
  description="What Bay Navigator does and does not measure about its visitors, and the data we publish openly."
  breadcrumb={[{ label: 'Transparency', href: '/stats' }]}
>
  <div class="ds-shell ds-stack">
    <h1>Transparency</h1>
    <p class="ds-lede">
      This page used to show a visitor dashboard. It cannot any more, because we stopped measuring
      visitors.
    </p>

    <section class="ds-section">
      <h2>We have no visitor numbers to show you</h2>
      <p>
        Bay Navigator loads no analytics script, no tag manager, no session recorder and no
        error-reporting agent. We set no cookies for any of those purposes. Until September 2026 we
        ran a self-hosted Plausible instance and published its dashboard here; that server was
        retired along with the rest of our self-hosted infrastructure, and nothing replaced it.
      </p>
      <p>
        So this is the whole truth of it: <strong
          >we do not know how many people visit this site, which pages are popular, or where anyone
          came from.</strong
        > That is a real cost. It means we cannot tell which programs people struggle to find, and we
        rely on people telling us instead. We think it is the right trade for a site that people reach
        during the worst week of their year, but it is a trade, not a free win.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our hosting and CDN providers keep their own server-side request logs, which we do not
        control and do not use to build profiles. That is described in the <a href="/privacy"
          >privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section">
      <h2>What we can open up instead</h2>
      <p>
        Transparency about our visitors is not available to us. Transparency about our data and our
        code is, and it is arguably the more useful kind:
      </p>
      <ul class="ds-stack">
        <li>
          <strong>Every listing we publish</strong> is available as open JSON{
            programCount ? ` — all ${programCount.toLocaleString()} of them` : ''
          }, alongside separate feeds for categories, service areas, crisis contacts and municipal
          code coverage. Start at <a href="/data/programs.json">/data/programs.json</a>, or read the
          <a href="/developers">developer documentation</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Every change is public.</strong> The site, the data and the scripts that maintain it
          are in one repository at <a
            href="https://github.com/baytides/bay-navigator"
            rel="noopener">github.com/baytides/bay-navigator</a
          >, including the commit that replaced this page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What we run and what it costs the planet</strong> is itemised on the <a
            href="/sustainability">sustainability page</a
          >, including the infrastructure we switched off and the one small service we still run.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What happens to your words</strong> if you connect Carl to your own AI assistant is
          spelled out in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and the <a href="/terms">terms</a
          >.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section">
      <h2>Found something wrong?</h2>
      <p>
        Since we cannot watch for problems in an analytics dashboard, being told is how we find out.
        If a program is closed, a phone number is dead, or a page will not work for you, please <a
          href="https://github.com/baytides/bay-navigator/issues/new"
          rel="noopener">open an issue</a
        > or <a href="/feedback">send us feedback</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="ds-eyebrow">Page last built {lastUpdated}</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
